    "facts_line": "2026-10-27 (Tuesday, before the open), 4 days out -- from the earnings calendar, consensus EPS 0.83.",
    "why": "Must show copper sales of at least 830M lbs at planned costs, so record prices reach earnings instead of being eaten by Grasberg."
  },
  "reasons": [
    "Copper set a record nominal high in May 2026, up about 20% year to date, yet Q2 revenue was 7.03B \u2014 up 12.8% from Q1 but 7.3% below a year earlier \u2014 because Grasberg volume, not price, is the constraint.",
    "Consensus is 0.83 versus 0.50 a year ago; FCX beat by 18.7% in July and the October 2 update already put Q3 copper production at 830M lbs, in line with plan.",
    "U.S. investor-owned utilities project more than $1.1 trillion of capex for 2025-2029, and 2Q26 plans were still expanding on data-center load growth; bill affordability is the overhang, not yet a cut."
  ],
  "watch": [
    "Copper sales versus the 830M lbs produced: at or above confirms the beat; a shortfall that pulls revenue under 7.4B breaks it.",
    "Unit costs: on plan confirms; another 5% overshoot like the third quarter's breaks the earnings conversion.",
    "Grasberg: guidance holding the end-2027 return to full capacity confirms; any slippage breaks the volume case.",
    "FY26 consensus EPS of 3.20: held or raised confirms; a cut breaks the 30-day revision trend."
  ],
